{"name":"Middle-Earth","hex":"#a2948d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Middle-Earth","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of Middle Earth.","Alternative letter-case form of Middle-earth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Middle-Earth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Middle-earth","blocks":[{"text":"Middle-earth is the setting of much of the English writer J. R. R. Tolkien's fantasy. The term is equivalent to the Miðgarðr of Norse mythology and Middangeard in Old English works, including Beowulf. Middle-earth is the oecumene in Tolkien's imagined mythological past. His most widely read works, The Hobbit and The Lord of the Rings, are set entirely in Middle-earth. \"Middle-earth\" has also become a shorthand term for Tolkien's legendarium, his large body of fantasy writings, and for the entirety of his fictional world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Baggins_residence_%27Bag_End%27_with_party_sign.jpg/330px-Baggins_residence_%27Bag_End%27_with_party_sign.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middle-earth","wikidata":"Q79734"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Vank_Cathedral%2C_Isfahan_-_Heaven%2C_Earth%2C_Hell.jpg/500px-Vank_Cathedral%2C_Isfahan_-_Heaven%2C_Earth%2C_Hell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Vank_Cathedral%2C_Isfahan_-_Heaven%2C_Earth%2C_Hell.jpg/1280px-Vank_Cathedral%2C_Isfahan_-_Heaven%2C_Earth%2C_Hell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Vank_Cathedral%2C_Isfahan_-_Heaven%2C_Earth%2C_Hell.jpg/500px-Vank_Cathedral%2C_Isfahan_-_Heaven%2C_Earth%2C_Hell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Medieval Christian cosmology: heaven above, earth in the middle, hell below.[1] Vank Cathedral, Isfahan.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVank_Cathedral%2C_Isfahan_-_Heaven%2C_Earth%2C_Hell.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}